# tools/blender holds the DKR track editor addon and tools/launcher-html the
# HTML/CSS/JS study of the launcher UI; both are tracked. Everything else
# under tools/ is not. Git does not descend into an excluded directory, so the
# directory itself must stay un-excluded for any rule inside it to apply - do
# not restore a bare /tools/ rule, it makes these folders invisible again.
/tools/*
!/tools/blender/
!/tools/launcher-html/

# Blender addon build output, rebuilt by tools/blender/package_addon.py
/tools/blender/dkr_track_editor.zip

# Built .dkrmap packages. These carry retail object-map data verbatim - the
# structure slot of a remix is the base track's map unless every object was
# moved - and docs/ASSET_POLICY.md forbids committing extracted maps. They are
# local test artifacts; rebuild them from Blender rather than sharing them.
/custom-tracks/
